Role Description
The Secretary-General’s Office (SGO) of the EFTA Secretariat services the EFTA Council and provides support and advice to the Secretary-General. It coordinates various horizontal activities in the Secretariat and provides legal advice, as well as statistical and economic analysis in support of free trade negotiations and policy development. SGO’s information and communication team is located in Brussels and works horizontally with all divisions, providing a wide range of services in communications and internal information and records management.
The Information and Records Management team is looking for a motivated and organised professional to support both the day-to-day operation of records management services and the implementation of a new records management system and digital archiving and preservation system.
Reporting to the Information and Records Manager, the Temporary Officer will contribute to records management, archiving, digital preservation, user support, project coordination and change management activities. The successful candidate will work closely with internal stakeholders to facilitate the transition to new systems and processes and support the effective management, preservation and accessibility of organisational information assets.
