Proven experience in delivering projects through the full life cycle;
Proven experience in supporting different stakeholders and cross-functional teams and engaging with third parties;
Strong interest in AI and exposure to its application in business contexts, including AI tools, use cases, or data-driven solutions;
Proficient skills in Microsoft PowerPoint, Excel (including formulas, pivot tables, and data analysis), Word, and Copilot;
Excellent command of English, both written and oral;
The following are considered a plus:
Experience as ScrumMaster or Product Owner;
Project management certifications (e.g. PMI, PM2, Prince2, SCRUM, SAFe);
Change management certifications (e.g. PROSCI, CLCA);
Experience in project portfolio management and/or project management office.
Key Competencies
Proactive and service-oriented mindset;
Critical-thinking, analytical and structured problem-solving skills;
Strong communication and presentation skills;
Ability to translate business needs into practical solutions;
Strong organisational and time management skills;
Champion for change and continually looks out for team and self-improvement opportunities;
Team-oriented, collaborative, and adaptable.
Application Process And Practical Information
Deadline for application: 28 August 2026;
Employment grade: Officer;
Contract duration: Four years, with possibility of extension;
Place of employment: Luxembourg;
